---
/**
 * /wallpapers/aesthetic — SEO landing page for the Aesthetic category.
 * Chrome page (ChromeLayout), fully indexable, links through to the real
 * photos at /gallery#aesthetic.
 */
import ChromeLayout from '../../layouts/ChromeLayout.astro';
---

<ChromeLayout
  title="Aesthetic Quote Wallpapers for iPhone | motivationalwallpaper.com"
  description="Soft, dreamy aesthetic wallpapers with gentle quotes for an easy, cozy lock screen"
>
  <h1>Aesthetic Quote Wallpapers for iPhone</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    A soft lock screen for the days you just want things to feel easy.
  </p>

  <p>
    Not every wallpaper needs to push you toward a goal — sometimes the
    nicest thing your phone can do is just feel calm to look at. This
    aesthetic category leans into lilac, mint, and petal-pink gradients
    paired with light, rounded type and gentle one-line quotes, the kind of
    lock screen that matches a cozy, unbothered mood rather than a
    motivational one. It's the category for a slow morning, a study
    session, or just wanting your phone to look like the version of your
    life you're curating.
  </p>
  <p>
    These wallpapers are popular for exactly what they are: pretty, easy on
    the eyes, and low-pressure. There's no discipline angle or grind
    energy here — just a soft, dreamy backdrop and a short line that says
    today gets to be gentle. If your other lock screens have been serious
    lately, this category is the palate cleanser: something that looks good
    in a screenshot and feels good every time you glance at it.
  </p>

  <p class="cta">
    <a href="/gallery#aesthetic">Browse the Aesthetic wallpapers &rarr;</a>
  </p>
</ChromeLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--t-title1-size);
    font-weight: var(--t-title1-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--t-title1-track);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--t-lead-size);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }
  p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .cta {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .cta a {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
